{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat","id":1550711,"title":"Running the Free States - 8 - the Sabbat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-05T18:05:45-07:00","id":1550711,"title":"Running the Free States - 8 - the Sabbat","content":"The Sabbat is interested in claiming southern California as well. Like Petrodon, they have their own agents there. So let\u2019s first cover the information provided in the LABN sourcebook itself.<br /> <br /> The most important is the undercover operative Mohammed al-Muthilim, the gang leader of the Sons of the Crypt. He rules a 25 man gang, the largest gang in Los Angeles. I believe a significant number of these - say five including himself - are true Sabbat, the others are just canon fodder he intends to convert or destroy once the Sabbat Crusade is unleashed.<br /> <br /> Another important undercover agent is Mariel St John, one of Fortier\u2019s lovers/brides. We\u2019re not given much background to her before her arrival in the Free States several years ago, but she was supposed to already be a well known vampire in LA when her book on the French &amp; Indian War was published. I assume she\u2019s originally Sabbat from Canada (it would help explain some of her own historical knowledge), but she had to have some kind of backstory that would not be suspicious. Ventrue do keep track of their lineages although I assume this is a bit harder for any Ventrue in LA itself. It would have been better if the sourcebook dealt with this a little bit, but I guess Ventrue do have cases of illegal embraces after all. If so, maybe \u201cMariel St John\u201d is the name of a mortal she killed and assumed her identity. If we assume Nightstar was an early Ventrue anti-tribu and that Mariel is also from Canada, it is possible Louis and his mistress are consanguineous.<br /> <br /> The other mention of Sabbat is a three Cainite pack in Simi Valley who appear to have just arrived there randomly and is not part of a coordinated plan. They are probably just some nomad pack taking advantage of a secluded area within the Free States. This is probably just an easy story hook so the PCs can destroy the Sabbat and gain some street credibility soon after they arrive in LA. It\u2019s probably what I\u2019ll do, so my design of the pack will be to showcase the bizarre features of the Sabbat. Showcase their inhumanity and bizarre ideology. Maybe show off a signature Sabbat Discipline like Obtenebration. But in the end, the PCs should be able to destroy them with a good plan and some help.<br /> <br /> = = = =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council\">Part 1 - the Anarch Council</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine\">Part 2 - Germaine</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance\">Part 3 - Governance</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs\">Part 4 - Canon Characters &amp; Gangs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites\">Part 5 - Setites</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla\">Part 6 - the Camarilla</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club\">Part 7 - San Francisco</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements\">Part 9 - Crossovers</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff\">Part 10 - Oddballs</a>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 02-02-2026, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T20:03:42-07:00","id":1550718,"title":"","content":"I'd work in some infiltration by the Sabbat. Sabbat's best recruiting tool is that they have an answer to impending wightdom. Have them convert a surprisingly high ranking Camarilla member by saving them from their upcoming wassail.<br /> <br /> If there's, for example, a Gangrel in the party, have a Sabbat Gangrel charm them by seeming like a nature-loving hippy, only to subtly move them closer and closer to following the Path of the Feral Heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T03:51:24-07:00","id":1550732,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not going to lie, Baron Fortier and one of his mistresses secretly sharing a \u2018Blood Mama\u2019 is exactly the sort of perverse-sounding, creepy-when-revealed Personal Drama that I want to see in VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE.<br /> <br /> Also, given that new recruits are being brought over on a regular basis, sometimes under irregular circumstances, and that Clan Records are extremely unlikely to be in a freely-available form (Much less digitised) it wouldn\u2019t surprise me if there were at least some wriggle room for an unfamiliar Ventrue to walk into a city and have at decent grace period to prove themselves a solid citizen (or not) before either being added to the appropriate records or subtracted from the population, presumably with extreme prejudice (Prince Vannevar Thomas and Baron Fortier himself present a precedent for this scenario).<br /> <br /> <br /> One important area of Anarch/Sabbat relations that seems<br /> underdeveloped is the Tiajuana/San Diego area - which, by dint of being one of the most populous areas on the Border AND a military hub is likely to be of extreme interest to both faction (Not to mention the Camarilla - after all, even the Ivory Tower sometimes needs the occasional \u2018windfall\u2019 from the back of an army truck and the Inner Circle would doubtless be even more keen to ensure that their rivals don\u2019t acquire insider access to the US Military.<br /> <br /> That the last local Prince vanished under somewhat mysterious circumstances and was replaced by Baron Tara Kearney, an outsider who came all the way from Texas (and in strength) during the Second Anarch Revolt also suggests at least two potentially-sharp plot hooks (With the Baron\u2019s canonical defection to the Camarilla at a later date suggesting a third).<br /> <br /> If nothing else, I suspect that tensions between those who\u2019ve been in the region since the days of Prince Maria and the Johnny-come-lately lot who\u2019ve seized power since (One can easily imagine the Tara working hard to ensure that vampire San Diego runs as a \u2018family business\u2019 whilst keeping an eye on the main chance all over the Free States, which would further elements of tension), complicated by their mutual desire NOT to be eaten by the Sabbat, are more plainly visible and visceral here than anywhere else in the Free States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T11:36:37-07:00","id":1550748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550718#post1550718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd work in some infiltration by the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there already is some quite high level infiltration of the Free State by the Sabbat, and as we'll see in some later points some other agents as well.<br /> <br /> I remember you almost exclusively run Sabbat games, so it'll be interesting to hear what you think the Sabbat should be doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550718#post1550718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sabbat's best recruiting tool is that they have an answer to impending wightdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is actually quite debatable. While the Sabbat do have alternative Paths of Enlightenment, I feel the vast majority of vampires already falling to the Beast under Humanity aren't going to do better under a Path of Enlightenment. It's like being told, &quot;Oh, you're having trouble with the philosophy of Aristotle? Have you tried reading Wittgenstein instead?&quot; I think only a relatively small number would actually succeed in being more successful under a Path, and most of those under the more relatively sane Paths like Honorable Accord or Power and Inner Voice than the more inhuman ones. <br /> <br /> However, I do agree that this is a pitch the Sabbat would make. Of course, someone close to falling to the Beast probably doesn't make the best recruit, but it's not like the Sabbat strategy already doesn't depend on cannon fodder. Another problem is that the anarchs absolutely hate the Sabbat. They see it as even more tyrannical than the Camarilla, and a lot have memories of either the 1965 Sabbat siege or are refugees from domains that fell to the Sabbat. This doesn't mean that there aren't vampires in the Free States who would be susceptible for recruitment for whatever reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550718#post1550718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have them convert a surprisingly high ranking Camarilla member by saving them from their upcoming wassail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is the Anarch Free States, this is hardly likely to happen or be convincing. While anarchs do have their own leaders, they are more likely to have achieved their position by merit, and someone who is incapable of staving off the Beast is unlikely to be well regarded. However, I imagine Mohammed al-Muthilim is able to recruit members of the Crypts secretly by offering to &quot;help&quot; someone struggling with the Beast through personal &quot;mentoring&quot;, and this is part of a long term process of building up Sabbat loyal members. He does need to be careful though because if exposed early, all his work goes down the drain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550718#post1550718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's, for example, a Gangrel in the party, have a Sabbat Gangrel charm them by seeming like a nature-loving hippy, only to subtly move them closer and closer to following the Path of the Feral Heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might run something like this as an individual plot for one of the PCs and see at what point - if ever - they figure out what's happening and likely destroy the Sabbat. My players won't be interested in turning their characters Sabbat, but they likely would have fun with their PCs being exposed to Sabbat practices in the chronicle. In any event, when the siege happens the Sabbat victory will depend more on the number of outside packs and covens show up combined with mass shovelhead embraces rather than internal recruitment of anarchs within the Free State.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat of my chronicle will be inspired by the original depiction, not the Revised era. So there is a lot more division within the Sabbat, and the Loyalists may not be dominant but remain a significant faction. I'm trying to think of ways I can incorporate the Loyalists into a Free States chronicle, as I imagine many Loyalists are very sympathetic to the anarchs of the Free States. This doesn't mean they would betray the Sabbat, but there's probably a fair number of Loyalists who would prefer MacNeil and the anarchs of the Free State over Lasombra and Tzimisce centralizers. I just haven't figured out an interesting way to present that to the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T12:44:38-07:00","id":1550753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550732#post1550732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it wouldn\u2019t surprise me if there were at least some wriggle room for an unfamiliar Ventrue to walk into a city and have at decent grace period to prove themselves a solid citizen (or not) before either being added to the appropriate records or subtracted from the population, presumably with extreme prejudice (Prince Vannevar Thomas and Baron Fortier himself present a precedent for this scenario).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that there must be some kind of probationary period to accept some unknown Kindred who claims to be, or appears to be, Ventrue. Something equivalent to the Probationary Sect Member flaw. The vampire probably needs to undergo the agoge to be accepted by the clan, no matter how many years they've already spent as undead. Perhaps be assigned a mentor while that is going on. Not just to educate them in the ways of the clan, but to determine whether they are infiltrators. Obviously it can't be perfect, but they have to have some success.<br /> <br /> I imagine Mariel would have needed to done that in some Camarilla city prior to arriving in LA so that she has some Ventrue bonafides. A convenient reason to leave for LA would not be hard to engineer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550732#post1550732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One important area of Anarch/Sabbat relations that seems underdeveloped is the Tiajuana/San Diego area</div> </div> </div> </div>Tijuana will play a role in the chronicle just as much as San Diego does. Tijuana was actually a very small city around 1945. It wouldn't get to around 100,000 people until the end of the fifties and was still under half a million in the early eighties. It's status as a growing major city doesn't really happen until the nineties. NAFTA had a lot to do with its spectacular growth. So at the time Tara seizes power, it's just another suburb of San Diego for all practical purposes and part of Tara's &quot;domain&quot;. Any vampires there would have to acknowledge of Tara's leadership. Most initially will be childer of Tara's coterie, but over time will attract native Mexican anarchs. Assuming she runs her domain much like a prince does, she probably has most of the checks and guards in place that one would find in similar Camarilla domains.<br /> <br /> I imagine the first Sabbat don't arrive in Tijuana until the time of the Sabbat siege of Los Angeles in 1944, and probably don't disrupt Tara's control of Tijuana until the mid-eighties. A significant background element in Rants will be requests for help for the &quot;Tijuana anarchs&quot; as Tara realizes the significant danger of a strong Sabbat presence.<br /> <br /> Since we established in the Germaine thread that he was active in Mexico, Tijuana might even be a good place for him to be even when he is not in LA proper. I'll have to create a dive gringo bar for him down there. He does have some connections with the Sabbat, but that doesn't mean he can't fight other members. I imagine his &quot;friends&quot; in the Sabbat are among the Loyalists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550732#post1550732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the last local Prince vanished under somewhat mysterious circumstances and was replaced by Baron Tara Kearney, an outsider who came all the way from Texas (and in strength) during the Second Anarch Revolt also suggests at least two potentially-sharp plot hooks</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the destruction of Maria, Prince of San Diego, is one mystery that doesn't have an easy answer in the LABN sourcebook. In the history section we're told &quot;two weeks later&quot; (presumably since Don Sebastian's destruction), Maria's servants found her staked and beheaded in a coffin, and then the anarchs swarmed in. In Tara's biography, we're simply told that Tara found Maria already destroyed when she arrived. It doesn't seem to be a secret then that Maria was already destroyed.<br /> <br /> We know most of the LA vampire elders were actually destroyed by the Lupines or Christopher Houghton, but neither of them had any reason to go down to San Diego. So who destroyed Maria?<br /> <br /> I think the simplest answer is simply the best. Finding a vampire in her coffin staked and beheaded is a classic scene of hunters destroying a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cZslXrOIS8o\" data-code=\"cZslXrOIS8o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/cZslXrOIS8o/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I imagine that's what happened here. It's just extremely convenient for the anarchs that it happened when it did. Approximately two weeks after December 22 is Three Kings' Day/Epiphany which marks the end of the twelve days of Christmas. Is that relevant? Or just a coincidence?<br /> <br /> One thing not really discussed in LABN (or indeed most city sourcebooks) are mortal hunters (outside of Reverend Cutler). Given SoCal's history as part of the Spanish empire with its Catholic missions and significant Catholic population, I'm going to put a major cenaculum of the Society of Saint Leopold somewhere. It might just be in San Diego (with a lesser one in Los Angeles). And yes, I'll follow the guidelines in 1995's Inquisition and make it a significant enough cenaculum that it has its own fax machine! I'll probably have one of its hunting groups based on John Carpenter's Vampires. I love James Wood in that movie.<br /> <br /> Since I hold that most hunters target Sabbat vampires because they are the ones most likely to not competently hide their activities, it's one reason why Tara does not have more trouble with the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T12:44:38-07:00","id":1550754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550718#post1550718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd work in some infiltration by the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there already is some quite high level infiltration of the Free State by the Sabbat, and as we'll see in some later points some other agents as well.<br /> <br /> I remember you almost exclusively run Sabbat games, so it'll be interesting to hear what you think the Sabbat should be doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550718#post1550718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sabbat's best recruiting tool is that they have an answer to impending wightdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is actually quite debatable. While the Sabbat do have alternative Paths of Enlightenment, I feel the vast majority of vampires already falling to the Beast under Humanity aren't going to do better under a Path of Enlightenment. It's like being told, &quot;Oh, you're having trouble with the philosophy of Aristotle? Have you tried reading Wittgenstein instead?&quot; I think only a relatively small number would actually succeed in being more successful under a Path, and most of those under the more relatively sane Paths like Honorable Accord or Power and Inner Voice than the more inhuman ones. <br /> <br /> However, I do agree that this is a pitch the Sabbat would make. Of course, someone close to falling to the Beast probably doesn't make the best recruit, but it's not like the Sabbat strategy already doesn't depend on cannon fodder. Another problem is that the anarchs absolutely hate the Sabbat. They see it as even more tyrannical than the Camarilla, and a lot have memories of either the 1965 Sabbat siege or are refugees from domains that fell to the Sabbat. This doesn't mean that there aren't vampires in the Free States who would be susceptible for recruitment for whatever reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550718#post1550718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have them convert a surprisingly high ranking Camarilla member by saving them from their upcoming wassail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is the Anarch Free States, this is hardly likely to happen or be convincing. While anarchs do have their own leaders, they are more likely to have achieved their position by merit, and someone who is incapable of staving off the Beast is unlikely to be well regarded. However, I imagine Mohammed al-Muthilim is able to recruit members of the Crypts secretly by offering to &quot;help&quot; someone struggling with the Beast through personal &quot;mentoring&quot;, and this is part of a long term process of building up Sabbat loyal members. He does need to be careful though because if exposed early, all his work goes down the drain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550718#post1550718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's, for example, a Gangrel in the party, have a Sabbat Gangrel charm them by seeming like a nature-loving hippy, only to subtly move them closer and closer to following the Path of the Feral Heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might run something like this as an individual plot for one of the PCs and see at what point - if ever - they figure out what's happening and likely destroy the Sabbat. My players won't be interested in turning their characters Sabbat, but they likely would have fun with their PCs being exposed to Sabbat practices in the chronicle. In any event, when the siege happens the Sabbat victory will depend more on the number of outside packs and covens show up combined with mass shovelhead embraces rather than internal recruitment of anarchs within the Free State.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat of my chronicle will be inspired by the original depiction, not the Revised era. So there is a lot more division within the Sabbat, and the Loyalists may not be dominant but remain a significant faction. I'm trying to think of ways I can incorporate the Loyalists into a Free States chronicle, as I imagine many Loyalists are very sympathetic to the anarchs of the Free States. This doesn't mean they would betray the Sabbat, but there's probably a fair number of Loyalists who would prefer MacNeil and the anarchs of the Free State over Lasombra and Tzimisce centralizers. I just haven't figured out an interesting way to present that to the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T15:08:27-07:00","id":1550766,"title":"","content":"If there\u2019s one thing I adore, it\u2019s Mere Mortals<br /> proving that even World of Darkness vampires, verily even Kindred with actual power, aren\u2019t as far out of their weight class as those vampires would like to be.<br /> <br /> Also, using John Carpenter\u2019s VAMPIRES as a model for World of Darkness vampire hunters makes complete sense: Mr James Woods and co are just sleazy and more than angry enough to work as underdog heroes OR gun for hire villains.<br /> <br /> It might be especially apt to introduce these hunters as a team rebuilding after being decimated by an especially nasty encounter with a vampire (\u201cNo, not that one, that one came later\u201d) as a tribute to the ending of VAMPIRES and a nod to the suggested turnover rate for vampire hunters in a setting/game line where vampires are the protagonists.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, is there any canonical information on the personality of Maria? (I quite like the idea that she\u2019s an escapee from the LA Toreador \u2018Boy\u2019s Club\u2019 - with the notion that Don Sebastian created no more than one female Childe due to his own Sire\u2019s fixations and that his own childer would be somewhat leery of Embracing women as a result of what they perceived to be the old man\u2019s prejudices - but not exactly a runaway).<br /> <br /> My take is that Maria, on some mission for the LA hierarchy, found San Diego an open city, saw the opening and set herself up as local Prince (In which assertion of praxis she was supported by the relatively small, mongrel rag-tag of local vampires, because with her Sire backing her from LA because this new establishment represented a growth in his own sphere of influence and the consolidation of his brood\u2019s status as members in good standing of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also fond of the idea that, due to the proximity of the Sabbat core in Old Mexico, Prince Maria tended to be a more lenient Prince than Don Sebastian - willingly accepting anyone willing and able to keep the Sabbat at a respectful distance, but ruthlessly cracking down on fools who might provoke the Sabbat without being able to substantially reduce their numbers - as well as the idea that at least one member of Tara\u2019s brood (Probably one of those who went their own way during the Civil War) was active in San Diego even before Kearney herself showed up (Suggesting a source of actionable intelligence on San Diego and the local Kindred).<br /> <br /> It has also occurred to me that one possibly-interesting variant on this notion would be to depict Prince Maria as somebody who got so tired of the LA boy\u2019s club that they decided to live as a woman once they got out from under Christopher, Don Sebastian et al.<br /> <br /> While this is based on the notion that Prince Maria was a Toreador, making the character a Nosferatu who got out of LA while the going was good and then decided that if the Clan Curse made it cursed near impossible for observers to tell whether they were even human or not, it was as good a reason as any for Maria to believe they could live as a woman, whether they started as one or not (With the power and prestige of a Prince making it all the easier for them to do so - an extra inducement for claiming the position).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T19:05:41-07:00","id":1550776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550766#post1550766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, is there any canonical information on the personality of Maria?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. <br /> <br /> It's important to realize like San Diego was not a very large city in 1945. It had only passed the 100k population mark sometimes in the twenties. The city was just above 200k in 1940, and all of San Diego county was 289k. In 1950 the city was 334k and all of the county was 556k. Even with the normal differences in the World of Darkness, there would not be a large Kindred population here. Probably just Maria, perhaps a few of her childer, and some independent vampires who recently moved there.<br /> <br /> Don Sebastian himself was only embraced in 1870, but as Prince of a rapidly growing city, he's certainly a candidate to be Maria's sire. The only thing against that is she'd be a very inexperienced neonate herself. At least Don Sebastian was supported and mentored by Christopher Houghton. The deserts of the American southwest just could not support a large population of Kindred in the early twentieth century and earlier. So it's equally unlikely any Princes of similar small cities in the region would have experienced childer either who would go there and rule. The only long term vampires who would be there are most likely Gangrel and possibly Nosferatu who were rural based and likely did not rule any urban areas.<br /> <br /> San Francisco would be the closest large city, but even here it only has a few decades head start on LA. Still by virtue of having one of the best natural harbors in the world and epicenter of the California Gold Rush, it would be the natural attractor for the first Kindred who wanted to head to the Pacific Coast and claim stakes. If Maria was a Kindred of some age and experience, she might have come here first. If she was someone locally embraced, she might still have a few decades head start on any other regional neonates who were ambitious. <br /> <br /> Still, any neonate attempting to become Prince would have to expect that the greatly growing cities of Southern California would attract competitors to be Prince. Lodin was a neonate when he became Prince, but he was of still potent generation, mentored extensively by TWO wise and powerful elders, and possessed a strong natural talent for politics. He did a lot better than he should for someone his age. Most neonate princes won't hold onto their title long once their city grows to a certain extent. An elder is going to move in and take over.<br /> <br /> So I imagine Maria would probably be at least be an ancillae or young elder who previously migrated to San Francisco (most likely) or Los Angeles, and wanted to try her hand at being prince by moving to San Diego in the 20s or 30s. I'd probably say she is most likely from Camarilla controlled Mexico who left when the Sabbat consolidated their control over that country during the Mexican Revolution and the burgeoning victory of the centralizers against the Loyalists in the Second Sabbat Civil War. (We should note that the population of Mexico overall was also quite small until its explosive population growth post-WWII. Outside it's Azteca/Purepacha heartland, most of it would be empty. She might be a descendent then of either Datura or Eletria of Veracruz, but could be from any unknown vampires. <br /> <br /> Maria does not need to be from Mexico despite her Spanish given name, but I think it's her most likely heritage unless she's even older and comes directly from Europe or old Spanish colonial cities in Latin America. Cities like Cartagena, Lima, and Bogota weren't very big, but they were so much older than Southern California cities and were likely settled by Kindred of potent generation. If you really wanted to have fun, you could make Maria a descendent of either Helena or Tyler who dwelled in Cartagena at some point.<br /> <br /> However, I actually don't think it's important where Maria came from. She's been destroyed for half a century at the time of LABN sourcebook, and she did not leave any legacy. She was likely only prince for one to two decades, and she's mostly a forgotten footnote. Regardless of who she was, there's no impact to the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Discussion of San Diego is perhaps taking up too much space on a thread meant for the Sabbat in the Free States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T11:17:05-07:00","id":1550803,"title":"","content":"Fair point. I admit to being fascinated by the \u2018also-ran\u2019 of history and (If memory serves) San Diego, whilst not very big for much of it\u2019s history, is the oldest European settlement in California - Presidio and Mission founded in AD 1769 - and even as early as the 1920s was site of some major investments in naval infrastructure (With millions of dollars flowing into the region and seven bases established), due to being one of the best natural harbours in the region.<br /> <br /> It also bears considering that while the Great Depression was doing a number on virtually everywhere, San Diego was experiencing actual growth (Not least due to the steady flow of \u2018Prohibition tourists\u2019 over the border to Tiajuana and back): it\u2019s also potentially of interest that San Diego was host to two World\u2019s Fairs.<br /> <br /> So while San Diego isn\u2019t likely to have a giant population of vampires, it might well have a surprisingly-old one (With the potential to make a good base of operations for a PC coterie during the Roaring Twenties - especially if we depict Prince Maria as a figurehead or make her one of the PCs).<br /> <br /> If nothing else, it might be potentially useful on a storytelling level to have somewhere we can point to as an example of how a Toreador prince could have handled the rapid expansion of their city during the period when Don Sebastian was sowing the seeds of the Second Anarch Revolt.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019ve rambled some more and apologise for being distracted from the Sabbat once again: please allow me to compliment you on your own suggestions for Prince Maria and thank you for your patience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T11:22:44-07:00","id":1550805,"title":"","content":"Anyway, regarding the Free States Sabbat, I tend to assume the most interesting angle to work would be an exploration of how similar and how very different the Sabbat &amp; the Anarchs can be - I believe that it\u2019s been mentioned in more than one thread that the Sabbat started out as art and part of the First Anarch Revolt, but grew more twisted with time &amp; internecine struggles, so what better place than the Free States to explore the gap between the founders of the Sabbat and the average shovel-head?<br /> <br /> (Also, what better way to put a hand on the shoulder of Anarch PCs and whisper \u201cAs you are, so we were - as we are, you may yet become\u201d?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T13:54:02-07:00","id":1550811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550805#post1550805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that it\u2019s been mentioned in more than one thread that the Sabbat started out as art and part of the First Anarch Revolt, but grew more twisted with time &amp; internecine struggles, so what better place than the Free States to explore the gap between the founders of the Sabbat and the average shovel-head?</div> </div> </div> </div>Players have a LOT more information about the setting than most characters should have. A lot of things that should be rare, esoteric, or forgotten lore seem to be thought of as routine character knowledge. Players who read the Sabbat sourcebooks know the entire history of the sect, but outside the Sabbat a lot of that should be unknown.<br /> <br /> There are also problems in that many players aren't aware of the actual history of the formation of the Sabbat and the importance of the Ravnos Methusaleh Vestgeir in transforming some of the survivors into the Sabbat. That is simply not mentioned in Revised and later sourcebooks. Many players erroneously assume the Sabbat appears almost fully formed soon after the Convention of Thorns. <br /> <br /> It's why I always default to what's in the original corebook as what information should be known to the PCs (at least those not of the Sabbat). If we go back the 2e corebook, this is what's known about the Sabbat.<ul><li>It's also called the Black Hand</li> <li>It originated as a medieval death cult</li> <li>Members worship at the places of the dead</li> <li>It requires strict devotion and adherence to the will of the group</li> <li>Sabbat initiation is designed to destroy any vestigial will in the new vampire</li> <li>They hold vampires holding onto their humanity to be blasphemy</li> <li>It is solely concerned with power in all its forms</li> <li>All who oppose them are burnt</li> <li>They ritually cannibalize their elders so younger, stronger, more aggressive vampires can take their place</li> </ul>That's what I tell any PCs what they know about the Sabbat. Now we can all see the hidden truths beyond these statements, but there is very little to suggest that the Sabbat has any origins among the Anarchs. I think very few anarchs know of any common origins. Sure, very elder anarchs like Robin Leeland know the story of the Anarch Revolt, the foundation of the Camarilla, and the Convention of Thorns. But even he knows nothing about how the vampires who rejected the Convention became the Sabbat. Robin himself would have been one of the anarchs who accepted amnesty and joined the Camarilla only to become dissatisfied later. <br /> <br /> I assume at most, Kindred may hear some statement about how only the worst criminals and cannibals of the Anarch Revolt rejected amnesty and were hunted down and destroyed. Decades later the Sabbat appeared, and it is likely those few surviving cannibals and criminals helped start it.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if you are some young Sabbat neonate, how much history do you really know? Or do you just believe that Caine founded your sect in order to defeat the rebellious and tyrannical antediluvians and their pawns in the Camarilla, and you need to exterminate them so you have a chance to survive? Does ancient history like the Anarch Revolt matter when the Sabbat has abandoned caring about its actual causes, and the important story is now about the destruction of two slumbering antediluvians? What does the Code of Milan have to do with freedom? Knowledge is power, and the Sabbat leaders would not want to give that up. The immense turnover of members in the Sabbat means very few have any recollection of the original Anarch Revolt or any access to someone who could (or would) tell them. For most Sabbat their history probably begins with the Revised Code of Milan and end of the Second Sabbat Civil War. Historical memory is oral. They don't have library books and internet articles to tell them independently what happened.<br /> <br /> Obviously there is still some historical memory left in the Sabbat, and the Loyalists carry the torch of the principles of the anarch revolt. They might try to find some kinship with anarchs, but I suspect many anarchs just view such statements as a ploy, and if they ask questions about what happened to cause the Sabbat to turn out the way it did, they'll receive some very unsatisfactory answers.<br /> <br /> Players might find it interesting to see the difference and parallels (even on these posts we see things like Caine and permitted diablerie come up), but I think the overwhelming number of anarchs would just reject the idea they have anything in common including origins. For anarchs who have little or no contact with the Sabbat, they might seem like a possible ally against a common enemy. For anarchs who have had contact with the Sabbat, they're just another enemy that needs to be defeated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T14:08:04-07:00","id":1550812,"title":"","content":"Not mentioned in LABN is any scout pack. Since my introduction to Vampire was through Chicago By Night, it\u2019s incredibly influential in my understanding of how things \u201cshould\u201d be done. In CBN there is a two person Sabbat scout team whose purpose is to observe, compile lists or all Kindred, determine their relative power, and avoid combat and being seen until the Sabbat invade. So that is what I usually do for a Sabbat presence in any non-Sabbat domain in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ll be adding (at least) two more Sabbat here. They duplicate some of what Mohammed and Mariel do, but redundancy and second opinions can be important. Plus there are some things that Mohammed and Mariel are not good for as it might blow their cover, but this scout pack can investigate. Just as the CbN scout pack did make contact with Tyler and other Kindred they thought they could recruit, this scout pack could do the same with Mohammed and Mariel (as well as contact other anarchs they think could be recruited as well). This pack is likely from Mexico since it is so close.<br /> <br /> We actually have an example of such a scout pack in Montreal By Night which has the Lost Angels pack. That pack was explicitly said to have performed \u201ccovert operations\u201d in LA during the eighties before they moved to Montreal, and their pack leader became Archbishop of Montreal. They include Carolina Velez, a stern, cautious, but politically savvy Lasombra from Mexico, and Gharston Roland, an LA native and former hitman embraced by a Ravnos anti-tribu (who was destroyed). Both are on the Path of Honorable Accord. The pack description seems to imply that after the failure of the Sabbat siege in 1965 that confrontations in LA between anarchs and scouting packs are an ongoing thing. The anarchs seem to be used to fighting Sabbat inside LA and are quick to do it.<br /> <br /> I wonder if that means I should introduce some kind of anti-Sabbat network and central coordinator among the anarchs. If someone sees something suspicion, contact this Kindred and leave a message. The anarchs need to determine if this mysterious Kindred is Sabbat or some clueless anarch newcomer. You want to deal with threats quickly, but since new anarchs from other cities arrive all the time, you hope to avoid destroying them by mistake.<br /> <br /> While I\u2019ve been long impressed by the creativity and mood of Montreal By Night, I think the NPCs are generally overpowered for their age. But it\u2019s the kind of thing one might expect from players who have had a lot of game sessions in a relatively short amount of IC time and want NPCs to be the same. It also has its own take on the Sabbat which differs some from the information presented in the original Sabbat sourcebooks. Still, there\u2019s a lot to mine there. I\u2019ll probably take a modified version of these characters, and possibly change names, so I can have a quick Sabbat scout pack to use.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T13:18:02-07:00","id":1550853,"title":"","content":"One other character you might consider taking a closer interest in is Julio Martinez - a Childe of Petrodon embraced at the time of the First Anarch Revolt (Possibly so that Petrodon had a spy who could insert himself into the First Anarch Revolt), then lost to the Sabbat when he became severely disillusioned with his sire after Petrodon exploited his Childe\u2019s capture by the Sabbat, rather than working for his release.<br /> <br /> Becoming an actual member of the Sabbat in time to become an early backer of Melinda Galbraith for the Regency of that sect, Martinez seems to be based out of Mexico City and presumably still hates his Sire even more than most Cainite do: it occurs to me that he might well regard the California Free States (His sire\u2019s particular focus) as an excellent vehicle by which to repay his grudges against Petrodon by proxy - presumably by doing his best to arrange things so that whether the Crypts eat the Anarchs from the inside or the latter continue to stand strong, Petrodon will continue to be cheated of his chance to bring the Free States back under the aegis of the Ivory Tower.<br /> <br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, it might be interesting to depict the \u2018Scout Pack\u2019 operating in the Free States as working at cross purposes to the Crypts and their master: after all, al-Muthilim wants to build and build his own power base whilst a Scout pack is almost certainly more hungry to find weaknesses and faults that will bring the LA crashing down, never mind whose power base might be wrecked in the process (Also, \u2018Papa Crypt\u2019 may well be eager to ensure that Sabbat intelligence on LA come only from HIM, whilst the Black Hand want some independent confirmation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T13:19:40-07:00","id":1550854,"title":"","content":"One question that occurred to me - is there any mention of where the Sabbat power bases/insurgencies nearest to Los Angeles can be found? <br /> <br /> We know roughly where the nearest Camarilla cities are, so what about their Cainite equivalents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T18:23:28-07:00","id":1550869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550854#post1550854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question that occurred to me - is there any mention of where the Sabbat power bases/insurgencies nearest to Los Angeles can be found?</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than &quot;Mexico is Sabbat&quot;, I don't think there's any development of nearby Sabbat strongholds.<br /> <br /> I imagine most people would say &quot;Tijuana&quot;, but I already gave my reasons for why Tijuana should be anarch or at least contested.<br /> <br /> While there are various cities in northern Mexico that would contain vampires, they are not particularly large. Mexicali and Ensenada in Baja California are under a million, as are all the cities of Sonora (including Hermosilla and Nogales). The state of Sinoloa is the same. The nearest &quot;major&quot; city that would be Sabbat would be the combined metro area of Ciudad Juarez in Chihuahua and El Paso, Texas. Their populations circa 1992 would be 790k and 515k (approximately 1.3 million).<br /> <br /> There are several mentions of Mexican anarchs in early Vampire sourcebooks, so the Sabbat is merely dominant in Mexico, not universal. Even Mexico City seems to have anarchs.<br /> <br /> For my own chronicles, I imagine much of northern Mexico - sparsely populated until quite recently - is much more anarch than Sabbat with the Sabbat dominant in the old Mesoamerican heartland (where most of the population is), and much less so outside of it. Since deciding that Germaine was once very active in Mexico, I am now much more leaning to make a larger anarch presence in Mexico than I would have previously.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T11:15:08-07:00","id":1550885,"title":"","content":"This strikes me as a situation that would help drive home the fact that while the Free States are Anarch, not all Anarchs are Free Staters - especially when they\u2019re on Sabbat soil.<br /> <br /> It strikes me as highly likely that the sort of Anarchs able to survive in Mexico are going to be extremely mobile, extremely good at hiding or very hard to tell apart from the Sabbat at a glance.<br /> <br /> Also, if I remember correctly the northern states of Mexico played a major role in the Mexican Revolutions &amp; civil wars, so it wouldn\u2019t surprise me if there are a significant number of nomadic packs and/or coteries which have taken a swing through the region at one time or the other (It\u2019s also plausible to imagine that this is the area Cainites who want to avoid getting chewed up in the latest faction fight, but don\u2019t want to desert the Sabbat, go to for a cool-down period*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Since there would be ample opportunities for murder and mayhem directed against rival factions, whether Anarch or Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T11:17:07-07:00","id":1550886,"title":"","content":"One other thought that occurs to me is that if Baron Tara Kearney and her following were famous Sabbat fighters back on the border, it\u2019s quite possible that some old enemies would go out of their way to pursue a vendetta all the way from Texas to San Diego (and possibly become a factor in Free States politics in the process).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T17:01:25-07:00","id":1550893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550753#post1550753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing not really discussed in LABN (or indeed most city sourcebooks) are mortal hunters (outside of Reverend Cutler). Given SoCal's history as part of the Spanish empire with its Catholic missions and significant Catholic population, I'm going to put a major cenaculum of the Society of Saint Leopold somewhere. It might just be in San Diego (with a lesser one in Los Angeles). And yes, I'll follow the guidelines in 1995's Inquisition and make it a significant enough cenaculum that it has its own fax machine!</div> </div> </div> </div>And while the stake and beheading <i>does</i> sound more Inquisition than government, I could see some Naval or Marine Corps Counterintelligence stumbling onto Kindred. Since this is before there was any kind of clearinghouse established for coordinated hunting, it could very well have been an isolated incident.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T20:47:47-07:00","id":1550898,"title":"","content":"I will be having a Revenant family be present in LA, although this is either unknown or unappreciated by the Sabbat involved in preparing the siege. I have a Zantosa estate in Mexico that controls one of the major Mexican drug cartels. That estate is a large ranch where they can raise horses to use for their own appetite for horseflesh. I'll have it be one of the large ones. They are involved in drug trafficking and sex slavery. I\u2019ll be using a Mexican family name vaguely reminiscent of Zantosa for the name of the cartel.<br /> <br /> The Zantosa are mentioned as being the wealthiest and most respected of the Sabbat Revenant families, but also mentioned is that they are no longer considered useful servants outside of extending hospitality to travelling nomad packs or covens. The Sabbat leaders have tired of their decadent games, at least in the original ST Guide to the Sabbat. Like a lot of things, the relationship between the Sabbat and the Revenant families have changed much between their original appearance and later sourcebooks, but I\u2019ll be going with their original description in my chronicle.<br /> <br /> As a result, the Sabbat will be neglecting the potential advantage the Zantosa crime cartel could provide them in LABN. Their presence in LA is more of an easter egg for the players if they should ever become involved in the LA crime world. Revenants can provide their own challenge to vampires so it\u2019ll be interesting to see if this leads to anything as a sandbox element. Because both Mohammed and Mariel don't come from Mexico or have previously established connections to the Zantosa, they'll be ignorant too. It is even possible that the Crypts could become gang rivals to the crime cartel as they are more likely to be connected to the Latin gangs in LA.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T09:24:52-07:00","id":1550956,"title":"","content":"I popped in here with the name \u2018Sartosa\u2019 on the tip of my tongue (Since it has that vague similarity to \u2018Zantosa\u2019 you were looking for), but a little research reveals that the Pirates of Sartosa are a WARHAMMER phenomenon and nothing to do with actual Spanish.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T09:26:25-07:00","id":1550957,"title":"","content":"I wonder if this family of revenants might originally have been drawn to the region by rumours of Christopher and the Nosferatu vampire who came into the region only slightly later, but hung around because they enjoyed getting a little distance from the bosses back in Mexico?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T13:20:40-07:00","id":1550970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1550957#post1550957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wonder if this family of revenants might originally have been drawn to the region by rumours of Christopher and the Nosferatu vampire who came into the region only slightly later, but hung around because they enjoyed getting a little distance from the bosses back in Mexico?</div> </div> </div> </div>While someone else can run with that concept into whatever direction they wanted, I have a far more prosaic reason. The original description of the Zantosa Revenants says their estates are located in North, Central, and South America. They keep stables because they like to eat horseflesh. Some are involved in the drug industry and slavery. That came together in my mind that one of the Zantosa estates are a ranch in Mexico where they control a cartel involved in drug trafficking and sex trafficking. That cartel is involved in Los Angeles because that's where the big money is. Nothing more. I may just name this fictional cartel the Durango Cartel because many Mexican cartels are named after the state they originate in.<br /> <br /> This group of Zantosa isn't native to LA. Their estate is probably located in Durango or Sinaloa where they originally were just large landowners and ranchers. When they became involved in the drug trade and sex slavery, the cartel inevitably expanded into LA since that's the largest market. Why did they involve themselves in crime? Simply as an outgrowth of their hedonism.<br /> <br /> The Revenants, of course, have an enormous amount of information about vampires so they have an advantage other crime groups don't have (not to mention their own Disciplines.) However, they know very little about LA's vampires and limit any investigations to strictly business. They don't want to attract attention to themselves, but do want to protect their operations from meddling vampires in LA. Yes, some individual revenants are either present in LA or occasionally visit operations there, but for the most part the cartel's operatives are all mortals.<br /> <br /> I intend this to be just a sandbox thing. Unless the PCs involve themselves in this kind of thing, I'll probably not make it a plot element. However, if for any reason they become involved for whatever reason, they'll make enemies of people who have tremendous knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T14:00:28-07:00","id":1551084,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m also going to mention the Red Listed Blood Brother, Angelo here from Kindred's Most Wanted, even though he actually is not part of the Sabbat sect. He was embraced by a pack of Panders in 1966 during the Sabbat siege of LA and then subjected to the Blood Brother experiments there as well.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t go into his details too much, but do want to mention that he was a mortal gang leader in LA, and he has local City Knowledge (Los Angeles) 5. Although he clearly travels all over the place, his backstory and city knowledge indicates he probably spends a lot of time in the Los Angeles area. Furthermore, most Camarilla Kindred who know of him think he\u2019s an anarch who kills an incredible amount of Kindred. The Tremere put him on the Red List because they noticed his strange aura and want a sample of his blood. They may be the only ones who claim he might be Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Despite the Tremere insinuating Angelo is Sabbat, this may be a case where everyone thinks this is another anarch on the Red List. Unlike Germaine though, it\u2019s not likely any anarch knows who this guy is because he's crazy and is incredibly dangerous to be around unless he thinks you\u2019re his \u201cbrother.\u201d<br /> <br /> Do the LA anarchs think he\u2019s a serial killer/criminal or anarch hero? Do any of the anarch leaders want to find and talk to him, just to know what\u2019s his deal? Has Germaine ever run across him (it\u2019s fun to consider that Germaine might know Angelo simply because he has met him on his own travels and he reminds Angelo of one of his \u201cbrothers\u201d, and thus doesn\u2019t kill him)?<br /> <br /> The fact that he has City Knowledge Los Angeles convinces me that I should include this character in LA at some point. I think I could have fun with Angelo for a story or two, especially if I have one of the PCs remind him of one of his brothers. This is an incredibly dangerous character with his maxed out stats and ability to control his frenzy. So this won\u2019t be a combat scenario (except possibly to conclude the story with either a whole mess of anarchs trying to kill him, setting him off against Sabbat, some other battle before he leaves the city, or having him become a wight). It\u2019s more about the mystery of who he is, and the realization he\u2019s a ticking time bomb.<br /> <br /> So not a sandbox element, but a potential short story/plot to use at some point down in the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T14:04:45-07:00","id":1551085,"title":"","content":"Given his name is actually \u2018Angelo\u2019 it wouldn\u2019t surprise me if he\u2019s seen as something of a living epitome of LA by the more jaundiced members of the Camarilla - heck, it\u2019s possible even some of his admirers call him \u2018Angelino\u2019 as a semi-affectionate nickname.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also morally certain that Smiling Jack and this jerk have made at least one horrible, horrible mess together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-17T23:58:13-07:00","id":1551113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1551085#post1551085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Given his name is actually \u2018Angelo\u2019 it wouldn\u2019t surprise me if he\u2019s seen as something of a living epitome of LA by the more jaundiced members of the Camarilla - heck, it\u2019s possible even some of his admirers call him \u2018Angelino\u2019 as a semi-affectionate nickname.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is possible some members of the Camarilla might consider &quot;Code Name: Angelo&quot; to be a nom-du-guerre with the purpose of letting people know his murder spree is &quot;From Los Angeles, With Love.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t9AeIdMQqR8\" data-code=\"t9AeIdMQqR8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/t9AeIdMQqR8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> If that spreads, the anarchs could keep it up. Of course, the leaders of the Anarch Council will be completely confused as to who this guy is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T13:10:35-07:00","id":1551349,"title":"","content":"I suspect that by this point the Anarch Council has become extremely accomplished in the noble art of shrugging off what doesn\u2019t actually foul their own nest\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T17:49:33-07:00","id":1551399,"title":"","content":"I found another old reference to a character! I thought about including it in the Canon NPCs thread, but felt it was of more relevance here. In the original 1993 Book of Madness sourcebook, it shows the Tremere anti-tribu infernalist Antonio d'Erlette. (The name is an obvious reference to the Lovecraftian character Comte D'erlette, author of the mythos tome Cultes des Goules. It was a reference to Lovecraf's correspondent August Derleth).<br /> <br /> The character's description is as a devoted infernalist responsible for recruiting many foolish and decadent nouveau riche of many eras. His ambition is to control the European Common Market (remember this was written back in 1993). Strangely he has no ranks in Finance, but does have Law 4. So he must be a lawyer, perhaps specializing in EU supranational law. Although he has many havens across Europe, he also has them in New York and Los Angeles. The man gets around!<br /> <br /> Going by the character sheet (written for Mage, not Vampire), Antonio has Dominate 4, Fortitude 2, Potence 2, and multiple paths of Thaumaturgy (highest is level 3). He is also given Arcane 5 which I'm going to translate into a combination of Obfuscate and a special demonic investment.<br /> <br /> While called a Tremere anti-tribu and thus indicating his nominal allegiance to the Sabbat, this Cainite is clearly more interested in and loyal to his demonic master than the Sabbat. For my purposes, he's essentially an independent Kindred with connections to the Sabbat. He looks Mediterranean and speaks with an aristocratic Spanish accent. He might be thought of as Mexican unless a PC knows enough Spanish to realize he speaks Castilian instead of Mexican Spanish.<br /> <br /> Considering his interests, he must spend most of his time in Europe, but the mention of a haven in LA means he must visit the city regularly, likely to tempt noveau riche mortals (especially new celebrities). Perhaps he specializes in actors who have or want second homes in Europe? He enjoys dirtying his hands and dislikes delegating anything he can do himself. So he's a good NPC to introduce plot directly into a chronicle!<br /> <br /> For my purposes, I can introduce this character anytime the PCs become involved with rich mortal celebrities. It'll be up to them if they discover he's 1) Kindred, 2) Tremere, 3) Sabbat, and 4) Infernalist (perhaps not necessarily in that order). He's powerful, but not that powerful, and he'll be by himself. He's also a way to introduce learning Thuamturgy or lore about the Sabbat depending on what the PCs do. He may also know of at least one of the deep uncover Sabbat agents of Los Angeles. It's likely the Sabbat does not know of his infernalist allegiance. If he does need help, he may try to get one of them to help him, not caring if he blows decades work of Sabbat intelligence gathering, only to save himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T09:06:13-07:00","id":1551543,"title":"","content":"I suspect that this fellow and \u2018Papa Crypt\u2019 would have some seriously Bad Blood between them (If only because he\u2019s exactly the sort of rival al-Muthlim could target with a clear conscience AND a serious chance of smearing the occasional rival by claiming they had somehow been associated with such a blatantly infernal influence).<br /> <br /> Heck, he could probably sell that line to the Anarchs AND The Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T16:56:54-07:00","id":1551550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat?p=1551543#post1551543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that this fellow and \u2018Papa Crypt\u2019 would have some seriously Bad Blood between them</div> </div> </div> </div>In many ways Antonio D'erlette is a &quot;strange&quot; Sabbat. Sabbat don't typically involve themselves in mortal society, yet this guy is trying to take over the Common Market! He also seems to be a loner rather than a member of a pack. He would make a much better Camarilla Tremere, yet since he needs to be an infernalist in order to be found in the Book of Madness, he must &quot;naturally&quot; be a member of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I imagine he must be some kind of high end troubleshooter for &quot;House Goratrix&quot; or perhaps the Lasombra. He is likely based in Madrid since that is the Sabbat's stronghold in Spain. Perhaps he even does things for Archbishop Moncada or another important Lasombra. The Tremere AT often serve as advisors or agents to Sabbat leaders, and being able to claim he is in service to a powerful Lasombra would help justify his worldwide travels. As a &quot;hands on&quot; kind of vampire, he would make a useful agent.<br /> <br /> So Antonio's presence in LA might make Mohammed believe that a powerful European Lasombra has her own designs in LA, and this represents an intrusion into what otherwise would be a New World (specifically Mexico based) Sabbat operation. But if he is an agent of a powerful Lasombra like Moncada, it gives him some political protection. Given that the Anarchs lack any real Tremere presence in the Free States, perhaps he poses as doing an independent inspection on what kind of thaumaturgy the anarchs would be capable of producing while he corrupts the souls of the newly wealthy in LA. Since Antonio doesn't actually care what happens in LA, Mohammed actually doesn't have much to complain about. Of course, that probably makes Mohammed think Antonio is just being exceedingly clever in hiding what he's really up to.<br /> <br /> Although it's mentioned that Antonio's sire was an infernalist who knew Gilles de Rais, we have no information on Antonio's own mortal life. I'm leaning to the idea that he is a relatively young vampire, and as a mortal lawyer was heavily involved in Spain's own accession to the EC and possibly involved in the post-Franco democratic transition. Since his sire was an infernalist, his embrace was probably done for the purpose of their demonic master rather than any Sabbat needs. (It's entirely likely most or all Tremere AT in Madrid then are secret infernalists.) Likely Antonio's sire provides some much needed magical protection against the very potent Tremere chantry in Toledo, and therefore is favored by the ruling Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T04:36:42-07:00","id":1551653,"title":"","content":"Making him a relatively young Cainite would also make it easier to believe that a Spanish vampire, apparently from an Establishment background, firmly committed to literally-Hellish practices would NOT regard an outspokenly-Islamic preacher with his very own home-grown, hand-picked <i>mujahideen</i> as a Priority Target (If only for the sake of his own Pride).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if his Sire is old and spiteful and Spanish enough, they may make it very difficult for their Childe to avoid making life as difficult as possible for a Lasombra who happens to be putting together his very own Muslim (Black Muslim!) power base in Los Angeles, California - if only so they can pursue Old Grudges in the New World.<br /> <br /> Admittedly it might be a stretch to identify \u2018Papa Crypt\u2019 as a Lasombra, but if anyone can do it \u2018tis a Tremere warlock with \u201cfriends on the other side\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}